      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T05:20:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "looks like you have to lock this mutex every time, so i wonder if it would hurt to have a static `Mutex\u003cOption\u003cBox\u003cbindings::file_operations\u003e\u003e\u003e` instead so that you need fewer statics + can skip the `UnsafeCell` stuff? if you lock it and see `None`, then you initialize it to `Some` and grab a pointer. if you lock it and see `Some`, then you just grab a pointer",
      "revId": "e5e83daa6c13121dc05d65a953b946e759d2b4d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac746469_e8daba48",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/shmem.rs",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 139,
      "author": {
        "id": 1892347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-07T12:34:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A `Box` inside a mutex can only be accessed while the mutex is held, but I need the pointer to remain valid even if I release the mutex. If we had a `OnceCell`, I could use that, but we don\u0027t have that in the kernel yet.\n\nI don\u0027t think it\u0027s a problem to lock the mutex for every `mmap` call; `mmap` is not a hot path.",
      "parentUuid": "f1eaf2f1_302e7084",
      "revId": "e5e83daa6c13121dc05d65a953b946e759d2b4d2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22dbd8f0_178e90c7",
        "filename": "drivers/staging/android/shmem.rs",
